      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona 22 August 2026 — Cardrona is open today, with winds easing a bit but still expected to make for an operationally challenging day — some lifts may be affected as conditions change, and snow showers are possible this afternoon. Currently 2°C with 40km/h winds gusting to 74. The grooming team laid down great cord overnight, and off-piste is firm for now but should soften as the day goes on. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Wells Pipe Platter are all running — Main Basin lifts and Valley View open from 8:30am, with Captains and T-Bar following at 9am, and Pipe and Platter aiming for 8am. Willow's Quad and its terrain are closed today due to the wind, and McDougall's won't be running gondolas, so no sightseeing today. Learners Slope, Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Arcadia Chutes and Summit are open, along with ski touring access, but Little Willows, Big Willows and Mt Cardrona are closed. Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane, Big Bucks, Olympic Pipe and Gravity Cross are all open in the park, while Peoples Pipe and Big Air remain closed. Today's Tots program has been cancelled. Please carry chains given the chance of afternoon snow showers. Carpark A is full, but B, C, the Yard, Valley View and the Pines all have space.",
